WEBVTT

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:03.940
Tokyo Sport University

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:06.860
Starting in ten,

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.320
nine, eight,

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:11.780
seven, six,

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.240
five, four,

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:17.490
three, two,

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:18.160
one!

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:35.970
<b><i>Run with the Wind</i></b>

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:08.670
They're going at a fast pace.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:09.460
Yeah.

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:10.860
Over here.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.400
Sorry I couldn't make the start.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.440
They just started.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.270
Kakeru's in the lead pack.

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:20.780
Wow.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.830
<b><i>Summer Prank</i></b>

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:33.000
Isn't Shindo waiting too long?

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:37.370
I think it'd be easier if he ran ahead.

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:38.470
What do you mean?

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:42.660
He tends to match the pace
of the people around him.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:44.930
It's exhausting trying to match
someone else's pace.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:47.300
I hope he doesn't pay for it later.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:50.000
Wow! You sound like experts.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:52.180
We're hardly experts!

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:54.280
What? Sure you are.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:05.740
Whoa, go!

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:06.850
Catch up!

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:08.700
Wow, wow! He's so fast! Wow!

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:14.010
Kakeru! Go!

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:21.230
Shindo moved up!

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.450
Their pace changed once they swapped places.

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:25.370
Why?

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:27.640
It's what they intended all along.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:30.460
Yuki sets the pace for the first half.

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:34.190
And Shindo pulls Yuki during the second.

00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:01.130
They planned their course
knowing they'd get lapped.

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:04.200
That must be Yuki's plan.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:05.420
It's so efficient.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:06.850
What's their time?

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:23.060
You like running?

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:27.740
Do you like running?

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:35.370
He caught up!

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:42.360
Kakeru! Go!

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:46.080
Wow! He's taking on the exchange students.

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:28.000
Isn't he a first-year?

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.230
He's from Kansei. Heard of them?

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:31.350
No.

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:36.580
Oh, shit!

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:38.200
He's crazy!

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:39.960
Haiji's next.

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:47.280
He's racing Haiji.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.860
He's not insolent for nothing.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:53.620
Haiji's moving up.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:57.560
Haiji!

00:05:57.560 --> 00:05:59.840
He conserved his energy.

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:02.700
Keep it up! Pull ahead!

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:12.480
You did it, Kakeru.

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:13.700
You got your revenge.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:20.780
Shindo, thirty more seconds!

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:23.440
Final spurt!

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:23.440
Yuki!

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:25.890
Shindo, you can do it!

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:26.490
Go, go, go!

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:37.250
You can do it! You can do it!

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:37.250
You got this. You got this. You got this.

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:37.250
Please, please, please.

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:57.020
Yes!

00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:21.790
Nice!

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:22.710
Yes! Yes!

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:24.090
Hey!

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:26.410
Get off me, it's hot!

00:07:28.570 --> 00:07:29.900
Hey.

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:40.530
Kansei University is an interesting team.

00:07:40.530 --> 00:07:43.150
I heard about you from Rikudo's Fujioka.

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:45.630
You're hoping to run at Hakone?

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:46.690
Yes.

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:52.880
It seems you still have members who 
haven't achieved the requisite official record.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:55.620
That's not a problem.

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:57.580
We have plenty more chances.

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:59.440
Yeah.

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:02.370
Anyway, you were outstanding.

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:06.090
Finishing in that time around this time
of year as a first-year is astounding.

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:07.760
Kurahara, huh?

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:10.460
Are you Kurahara of Sendai Josei High School?

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:17.580
Hey, he asked you a question.

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:18.510
I'm sorry.

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:20.610
Our friends are waiting.

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:22.310
Let's go.

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:27.340
I'll be back to interview you properly.

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:30.480
<b>Shinjitsu Weekly
Mochizuki Shuji</b>

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:30.480
I'm Mochizuki of Shinjitsu Weekly magazine.

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:31.920
Excuse us.

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:50.990
Hey!

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:53.670
<b>Chikusei-so</b>

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:53.120
Somen's almost ready.

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:57.430
I'd rather have air conditioning than noodles...

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:59.050
Air conditioning...

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:02.430
Quit complaining and bring me a shiso leaf.

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:05.250
I thought I'd be glad the rainy season was over.

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:08.260
Apparently, this is the hottest
summer in recorded history.

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:10.070
I'm amazed we're not dead.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:14.080
If you don't eat, you really will die
during evening practice.

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:15.300
First semester is over.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:16.960
It's summer break, everyone.

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:19.200
What are you doing?

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:22.610
It's them. The pair that never fails a class.

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:28.490
We're destined to end up on
Nico-chan Senpai's side of life.

00:09:28.490 --> 00:09:30.890
Welcome to my side.

00:09:30.890 --> 00:09:31.960
Where are the others?

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:34.020
I haven't seen them.

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:35.860
Haiji's not here either?

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:36.680
Nah.

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:39.390
Whatever. Let's eat without them.

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:42.430
We've been eating nothing but somen lately.

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:45.350
Who cares? It's too hot to think.

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:49.760
I wish we could go someplace
cool, like Hokkaido.

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:54.010
Hokkaido?!

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:08.330
Hokkaido sounds nice.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:10.860
Hey.

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:15.150
Reality just came charging in.

00:10:15.150 --> 00:10:18.410
We're escaping from this scorching hell.

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:19.550
Escaping?

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:21.510
A training camp!

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:23.470
A summer training camp!

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:28.890
To Hokkaido?!

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:30.450
To Lake Shirakaba!

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:38.150
Why did you choose the mountains?

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:43.960
The owner of the batting cage
in the shopping center

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:46.780
said we could borrow their villa.

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:51.120
And the people at the shopping
center provided us with groceries.

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:57.090
Why does this guy get a seat
when I have to sit in the back?

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:58.700
It can't be helped.

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:01.090
You're the one who lost rock-paper-scissors.

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:03.370
I'm excited about the lake.

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:05.460
Face forward!pp

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:12.000
This is awesome.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:14.180
Even the breeze is starting to feel moist.

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:25.520
No!

00:11:28.050 --> 00:11:29.960
Escaping the heat, huh?

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:34.420
But I'm supposed to be the coach...p

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:52.210
Well, this is reality.

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:54.550
Let's start by cleaning.

00:11:54.550 --> 00:11:55.660
Um...

00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:59.650
Could we wash ourselves off
in the river first?

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:05.280
It's cold once the sun goes down.

00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:08.130
Okay, it's ready.

00:12:08.130 --> 00:12:10.030
All that's left is to mix in the roux.

00:12:10.030 --> 00:12:12.850
Curry already? What a cliché.

00:12:12.850 --> 00:12:14.610
All that's left is to mix it in?

00:12:14.610 --> 00:12:16.760
Then quit putting on airs and mix it in already.

00:12:16.760 --> 00:12:17.960
What are you talking about?

00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:20.330
We're going for a run before dinner.

00:12:20.330 --> 00:12:22.210
What?!

00:12:22.210 --> 00:12:26.970
I don't mind having a soup of potatoes
and carrots boiled in plain old water.

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:30.030
You can really enjoy
the flavors of the ingredients.

00:12:30.450 --> 00:12:33.230
And of course, I'm the only one
who knows where the roux is.

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:36.480
Hurry up.

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:38.980
You don't want to get attacked
by a bear at night.

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:42.320
<b>Beware of Wildlife</b>

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:41.420
We're still in hell!

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:45.530
Head down the hill, 
and you'll reach the lake.

00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:49.300
The lake is 3.8 kilometers around.

00:12:49.300 --> 00:12:52.040
You can return to the villa 
once you've completed three laps.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:54.000
Okay.

00:12:53.650 --> 00:12:56.710
<b>Shinanoji Footpath

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:03.240
We're here. It's the lake.

00:13:16.100 --> 00:13:17.730
Kurahara, huh?

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:21.480
Are you Kurahara of Sendai Josei High School?

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:41.050
All right!

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:46.340
<b>Glutamine, vitamin B group,
minerals (Ca, Mg, Fe)
</b>

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:46.340
<b>100% whey protein for building 
an athlete's body</b>

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:46.340
<b>Strawberry flavor</b>

00:13:44.530 --> 00:13:47.340
Hold on! What are you doing with that?

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:50.100
But you said it was cliché.

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:52.370
Cliché is fine! Cliché is good!

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:54.630
What? Let's just try it.

00:13:53.120 --> 00:13:53.930
Excuse me...

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:54.990
Huh?

00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:56.450
I'm telling you, don't do it!

00:13:54.990 --> 00:13:56.540
Aren't we missing something?

00:13:56.450 --> 00:13:57.330
What?

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:59.620
What? This should be plenty.

00:13:57.330 --> 00:13:59.620
No!

00:13:59.620 --> 00:14:01.190
Just how much are you going to eat?

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:02.360
That's not what I meant.

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:04.860
I meant, isn't someone missing?

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:08.200
I'm exhausted.

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:10.910
Huh? It's not bad.

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:13.370
We're out.

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:16.070
Curry! Curry!

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:20.950
Musa.

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:22.880
And Shindo.

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:28.590
I can't see anything.

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:31.260
Maybe we shouldn't be wandering around.

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:33.720
But it's so cold.

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:36.240
What if they've fallen 
into a ravine and gotten stuck?

00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:38.100
Don't say that.

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:40.260
Do you think they have their phones?

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:42.870
Even if they do, they won't have any bars.

00:14:42.870 --> 00:14:44.350
Calm down, guys.

00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:46.550
Let's split into two groups.

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:49.650
Some of us will stay here, and the rest
of us will use the van to look for them.

00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:51.900
I'll stay here.

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:57.080
<b>Beware of Wildlife</b>

00:14:52.590 --> 00:14:55.980
I said two groups. 
Why do you all want to stay?

00:14:59.680 --> 00:15:01.500
What was that?

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:04.140
A wild animal?

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:07.220
It's coming closer.

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:10.700
Calm down.

00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:12.890
This calls for...

00:15:27.890 --> 00:15:30.610
They ran into the van.

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:36.910
Shindo possesses incredible talents.

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:41.430
He easily climbs up steep mountainsides
and uses the stars to find his way.

00:15:41.430 --> 00:15:42.290
Aw, shucks.

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:43.960
"Aw shucks"?!

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:45.840
We were worried about you.

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:48.220
I'm honestly mystified you're not injured.

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:50.170
I'm sorry.

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:53.520
We found a path on the edge of the lake.

00:15:53.520 --> 00:15:56.140
We thought it'd be perfect
for cross country running,

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:57.860
but once we followed it, we got lost...

00:15:57.860 --> 00:15:59.780
I'm glad you're all right,

00:15:59.780 --> 00:16:04.280
but if this were Hakone, you'd be
disqualified for leaving the course.

00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:05.470
Yes, sir.

00:16:05.470 --> 00:16:07.260
Isn't there a lead car?

00:16:07.260 --> 00:16:09.270
Oh. Come to think of it...

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:10.080
Right?

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:13.090
Yes, I was surprised.

00:16:13.090 --> 00:16:15.730
Apparently, Tokyo Sport Uni is here, too.

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:17.280
What?!

00:16:18.730 --> 00:16:21.950
We were drawn out of the
bushes towards the light.

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:25.130
It was a beautiful building.

00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:27.200
They were grilling meat.

00:16:28.140 --> 00:16:32.080
Entrails, liver, spare ribs, sirloin...

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:34.800
I'd recognize that marbling anywhere.

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:37.860
That was Japanese black wagyu beef!

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:45.210
There's no meat in this.

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:50.280
<b>Shirakaba Loop</b>

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:50.150
Group A, start!

00:16:54.340 --> 00:16:56.790
I can't believe we ran into them.

00:16:56.790 --> 00:16:58.620
They're kind of amazing.

00:16:59.020 --> 00:17:01.110
It's like they're a real track team.

00:17:01.110 --> 00:17:03.020
We're a real track team, too.

00:17:03.020 --> 00:17:04.290
Group B, start!

00:17:05.910 --> 00:17:07.320
Group C, stand by!

00:17:09.220 --> 00:17:10.710
Last ones, group D!

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:12.520
Don't make them wait!

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:24.730
It's difficult to run like this.

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:27.660
Aren't they spreading out more than necessary?

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:29.790
Our pace is dropping. Let's go faster.

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:32.070
Hey, don't do anything stupid.

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:34.160
Then why are we holding this training camp?

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:37.920
Everyone, maintain your own pace.

00:17:38.310 --> 00:17:39.160
Haiji!

00:17:39.650 --> 00:17:41.410
Didn't you hear me?

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:44.030
I told everyone to maintain their own pace.

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:53.840
Hey!

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:55.940
No one has that much energy in the morning.

00:17:55.940 --> 00:17:58.910
I'm worried about him going off
on his own. I'm going with him.

00:17:58.910 --> 00:17:59.850
Okay.

00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:07.480
<b>Shirakaba Loop</b>

00:18:13.060 --> 00:18:14.400
The air is beautiful.

00:18:15.510 --> 00:18:17.520
It makes me happy just to breathe.

00:18:19.250 --> 00:18:20.720
Don't you agree?

00:18:26.210 --> 00:18:29.120
Feel the wind. Maintain your rhythm.

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:32.670
This is training, too.

00:19:10.810 --> 00:19:12.120
How childish.

00:19:14.260 --> 00:19:15.480
What?

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:16.770
We're in the way?

00:19:16.770 --> 00:19:18.970
We aren't getting the way. Right?

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:19.670
Right.

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:21.690
They're just picking a fight.

00:19:21.690 --> 00:19:25.750
Let's go. We still have training left to finish.

00:19:25.750 --> 00:19:27.730
I understand your position.

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:29.440
I'm not going to talk to your coaches.

00:19:30.360 --> 00:19:32.080
I'd just be happy to have your understanding.

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:35.520
Oh, we understand.

00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:37.560
We're serious about this.

00:19:37.560 --> 00:19:40.710
We don't have time for pleb teams.

00:19:40.710 --> 00:19:41.910
Pleb?

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:44.050
You'll be the center of attention if you run.

00:19:44.050 --> 00:19:46.220
People will talk about you
if you say you want to run.

00:19:46.610 --> 00:19:50.800
I'm talking about plebs
who set unrealistic goals

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:53.330
on the basis of such shallow thinking.

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:54.980
Yikes.

00:19:57.890 --> 00:20:00.170
I know. Why don't we race?

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:02.840
Just us first-years, ten against ten.

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:06.410
Then you'll see what it means to be serious.

00:20:06.410 --> 00:20:07.900
Race me, then.

00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:10.870
I'm the only one who needs to.
They have nothing to do with this.

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:15.480
That's how you break a team.

00:20:17.170 --> 00:20:18.370
Break?

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:22.400
Get good times, receive attention.

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:24.400
You don't feel bad about it, do you?

00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:27.080
And you forget about the
sacrifices other people made.

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:28.870
What's he talking about?

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:30.830
We won't race you.

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:34.890
There's not much to gain
from racing against children.

00:20:34.890 --> 00:20:36.000
Let's head back.

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.840
We're wasting time.

00:20:38.820 --> 00:20:42.720
Are you satisfied running 
with the friends you finally made?

00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:47.880
Are you satisfied holding hands and
running around with your little friends?!

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:55.940
Kakeru!

